      "created_at": "2017-12-12T13:32:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-12-12T13:32:46Z",
      "body": "There is no other solution than to use the filter. \r\n\r\nIf you won't ever have U.S./Canadian addresses, then the filter is very simple and you can simply return a HTML like `<option value=\"-\">---</option>`.\r\n\r\nIf you need to handle U.S./Canadian addresses also, then I would suggest copying the `state-and-province-dropdown.php` file, adding the change you suggested, and running a filter function like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nadd_filter( 'yikes-mailchimp-state-province-list', 'my_own_state_province_list', 10, 2 );`\r\n\r\nfunction my_own_state_province_list( $html_list, $form_id ) {\r\n    return PATH/TO/MY/VERSION/OF/STATE/AND/PROVINCE/LIST\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nDoes that make sense? \r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nKevin.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
